window.GW_LEGAL = {"meta": {"owner": "Elite Chess", "law": "Victoria, Australia", "effective": "18 October 2026", "year": "2026", "contact": ""}, "terms": "<p class=\"lg-date\">Effective 18 October 2026</p>\n<p>These Terms of Use (“Terms”) are an agreement between you and Elite Chess (“we”, “us”, “our”) about your use of the Elite Chess app for Android,\nthe website elitechess.online, the single-file offline copy, and every feature, update and piece of content in them (together, the “Service”).\nBy downloading, opening or using the Service you agree to these Terms and to our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.</p>\n\n<h3>1. Who may use the Service</h3>\n<ul><li>Anyone may play on their own device, including in kids mode.</li>\n<li>Online play, friends, tournaments and accounts are for people aged 13 or over. If you are under 18, you must have a parent or guardian’s permission, and they are responsible for your use.</li>\n<li>You must not use the Service if the law where you live forbids it.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>2. Your licence to use the Service</h3>\n<p>We grant you a personal, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable and revocable licence to install and use the Service on devices you own or control,\nfor your own private, non-commercial enjoyment of playing and learning chess. Everything not expressly granted is reserved by us. The Service is licensed to you, not sold.</p>\n\n<h3>3. What belongs to us</h3>\n<p>The Service and everything in it, other than the third-party parts listed under Legal → Credits, is owned by Elite Chess and protected by the <i>Copyright Act 1968</i> (Cth),\nthe <i>Trade Marks Act 1995</i> (Cth), the law of confidential information and passing off, the Australian Consumer Law, and international treaties. This includes, without limitation:</p>\n<ul><li>the software, source code, object code, scripts, file structure and build tools;</li>\n<li>every character and piece set we created, including the holiday and seasonal sets, the sports sets and the Tournament Wood set, each individual piece, their names, poses and animations;</li>\n<li>the animated scenes and flyovers (for example the sleigh, witch, dragon and race-car scenes), boards, board themes, textures, colourways, icons, avatars and illustrations;</li>\n<li>the bot characters, their names, descriptions and playing styles; lessons, courses, explanations, quizzes, opening guides, our own puzzles and all other text;</li>\n<li>sound mixes, the user interface and its overall look, layout, sequence and feel;</li>\n<li>the selection, arrangement and compilation of all content, including data compilations; and</li>\n<li>the names “Elite Chess”, “Tournament Wood”, our logo and app icon (our trade marks).</li></ul>\n\n<h3>4. What you must not do</h3>\n<p>Unless we have given you written permission, or a law that cannot be excluded allows it, you must not, and must not help anyone else to:</p>\n<ul><li>copy, reproduce, download for reuse, record, screenshot for reuse, republish, distribute, sell, rent, lend, license or otherwise make available any part of the Service;</li>\n<li>take, trace, redraw, imitate, adapt or reuse any of our characters, piece sets, pieces, boards, artwork, animations, themes, icons, sounds or text, in whole or in part, including making “inspired by” versions that are substantially similar;</li>\n<li>make derivative works or merchandise from our content, including prints, clothing, stickers, physical or 3D-printed chess sets, 3D models, game assets, NFTs or digital collectibles;</li>\n<li>use any part of the Service in another app, game, website, video, stream thumbnail, advertisement or product, except ordinary personal sharing of your own games and screenshots that show the Elite Chess name;</li>\n<li>clone, mirror, frame, re-host or re-skin the Service, or rebuild, repackage, re-sign or republish the app, its APK, the offline copy or the website, under any name;</li>\n<li>decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer, de-obfuscate or try to derive source code, except to the extent the <i>Copyright Act 1968</i> (Cth) or an open-source licence for a third-party part expressly permits it;</li>\n<li>remove, hide or change any copyright notice, trade mark, credit, licence notice or this Terms link;</li>\n<li>scrape, crawl, spider, harvest or bulk-download the Service or its data, or access it by any automated means other than a normal web browser or our app;</li>\n<li>use any part of the Service, including our art, characters, text or code, to train, fine-tune, test or prompt any artificial intelligence or machine-learning system, or to generate look-alike content;</li>\n<li>use “Elite Chess” or any of our trade marks, or a confusingly similar name, logo, domain, app title or social media handle, or suggest that you are connected with us;</li>\n<li>get around, disable or interfere with security features, the update and integrity checks, or any limit on use;</li>\n<li>hack, overload, probe or disrupt the Service or the services it connects to, or introduce malware;</li>\n<li>cheat in online play or tournaments (including using an engine, another person or any outside help), manipulate ratings or results, or use bots;</li>\n<li>choose a name or profile that is offensive, misleading or impersonates someone, or harass, threaten or abuse other players; or</li>\n<li>use the Service for anything unlawful, or in a way that infringes anyone’s rights.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>5. Open-source and third-party parts</h3>\n<p>Some parts of the Service are made by others and are used under their own licences, which are listed with their full texts in the app under Legal → Credits.\nThese include the Stockfish chess engine (GNU GPL v3) and several optional piece sets. Those licences govern those parts, and nothing in these Terms restricts any\nright that an open-source licence gives you, including your right to obtain, study, change and share Stockfish under the GPL. The restrictions in section 4 apply to everything else.</p>\n\n<h3>6. Online play and fair play</h3>\n<p>Online games, friends and tournaments connect your device directly to other players’ devices. Play fairly and respectfully. We may remove, block or ban anyone\nwho breaks these Terms, and we may cancel results that were obtained unfairly. We do not check or control other players and are not responsible for what they do.</p>\n\n<h3>7. Your content</h3>\n<p>You keep any rights you have in the name, avatar and other details you enter. You let us store, copy and show them to run the Service (for example, showing your name to an opponent).\nChess moves and results are facts and are not owned by anyone.</p>\n\n<h3>8. Ideas and feedback</h3>\n<p>If you send us ideas or feedback, you agree that we may use them freely, without paying you or giving you credit.</p>\n\n<h3>9. Information from others</h3>\n<p>Live sports scores, chess rankings, events and similar information come from third parties. They are shown for general information only and may be delayed,\nincomplete or wrong. Names of leagues, events, teams and players belong to their owners and are used only to identify them. We are not affiliated with,\nsponsored or endorsed by any of them. Links to other websites are not under our control.</p>\n\n<h3>10. Paid features</h3>\n<p>If we offer paid features, the price and what you get will be shown before you pay. Payments made through an app store are also subject to that store’s terms.\nYour rights under the Australian Consumer Law are not affected.</p>\n\n<h3>11. Changes, updates and availability</h3>\n<p>We may change, update, suspend or stop any part of the Service at any time. The app updates itself automatically from elitechess.online. We do not promise that the Service will always be available,\nerror-free or compatible with your device.</p>\n\n<h3>12. Ending your licence</h3>\n<p>You may stop using the Service at any time. If you break these Terms, your licence ends automatically and immediately. When it ends you must stop using the Service and delete every copy of it and of our content.\nSections 3, 4, 5 and 13 to 17 continue after it ends.</p>\n\n<h3>13. Protecting our rights</h3>\n<p>We actively protect our work. If you break section 4, we may, without notice, block your access, report the matter to app stores, hosting providers, marketplaces and payment providers,\nand take legal action anywhere in the world for an injunction, damages or an account of profits, delivery up or destruction of infringing copies, and our legal costs.\nA breach of section 4 may cause us harm that money alone cannot fix, so we may seek urgent court orders.</p>\n\n<h3>14. Australian Consumer Law</h3>\n<p>Our goods and services come with guarantees that cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law. Nothing in these Terms excludes, restricts or changes any right or remedy\nyou have under the Australian Consumer Law or any other law that cannot be excluded. Where we are allowed to limit our liability for a failure to meet a guarantee,\nour liability is limited, at our option, to supplying the services again or paying the cost of having them supplied again.</p>\n\n<h3>15. Disclaimer and limit of liability</h3>\n<p>To the extent the law allows, the Service is provided “as is” and “as available”, without any other promise or warranty. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect or\nconsequential loss, loss of data, profits or opportunity, and our total liability to you for all claims is limited to the greater of AUD 100 or the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim.</p>\n\n<h3>16. Your responsibility</h3>\n<p>To the extent the law allows, you agree to cover our reasonable losses and costs (including legal costs) caused by your breach of these Terms or your infringement of anyone’s rights.</p>\n\n<h3>17. Law and courts</h3>\n<p>These Terms are governed by the law of Victoria, Australia. You and we submit to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Victoria and the Commonwealth of Australia.\nWe may also bring proceedings to protect our intellectual property in any country where an infringement happens.</p>\n\n<h3>18. General</h3>\n<p>If any part of these Terms is invalid, the rest still applies, and the invalid part is read down or removed only as much as needed. If we do not enforce a term straight away,\nwe can still enforce it later. You may not transfer your rights under these Terms; we may transfer ours. These Terms, the Privacy Policy and the Copyright notice are the whole agreement about the Service.</p>\n\n<h3>19. Changes to these Terms</h3>\n<p>We may update these Terms. The new version applies from the date shown at the top once it is published in the Service or on elitechess.online. If you keep using the Service, you accept the new version.</p>\n\n<h3>20. Contact</h3>\n<p>Questions or notices about these Terms: the contact address published on this page (a dedicated address for notices is being set up; until then, watch elitechess.online for it).</p>", "privacy": "<p class=\"lg-date\">Effective 18 October 2026</p>\n<p>This Privacy Policy explains how Elite Chess (“we”) handles personal information in the Elite Chess app, the website elitechess.online and the offline copy (the “Service”).\nWe follow the Australian Privacy Principles in the <i>Privacy Act 1988</i> (Cth), and we respect the rights of users in other places, including the EU and UK.</p>\n\n<h3>The short version</h3>\n<ul><li>No advertising, no analytics, no tracking cookies, and we never sell your information.</li>\n<li>Your profile, settings, progress and games are stored on your own device.</li>\n<li>Online play connects you directly to the other player’s device, which means they can see your internet (IP) address.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>1. Information on your device</h3>\n<p>Your display name, avatar, country (if you choose one), settings, progress, puzzles, achievements, saved games and friends list are stored in your browser or app storage on your device.\nWe do not receive them unless you sign in to an account (section 3). You can delete them with Settings → Reset all progress, or by clearing the app’s or browser’s data.</p>\n\n<h3>2. Online play, friends and tournaments</h3>\n<p>When you play online, add friends or join a tournament, the Service uses the PeerJS connection service to introduce your device to the other player’s device, and then connects the two devices directly (WebRTC).\nTo do this, your device shares with the other players and with the connection service: your display name, avatar, country flag, rating, friend code, your moves and game details, and your device’s internet (IP) address.\nThe other player’s device can therefore see your IP address, which can show your approximate location. If you do not want this, do not use the online features.</p>\n\n<h3>3. Accounts (when available)</h3>\n<p>If you create an account, we use Google Firebase (Authentication and Firestore) to sign you in and to keep your progress in step across devices. Firebase stores your email address,\nan account ID, your sign-in details and a copy of your progress. If you sign in with Google, Google shares your name, email address and profile picture with us. Firebase servers may be outside Australia, including in the United States.</p>\n\n<h3>4. Other services the Service connects to</h3>\n<ul><li><b>Hosting and updates:</b> the website and app updates are served by GitHub Pages. Like any web server, it receives your IP address and basic browser details when it serves files.</li>\n<li><b>Live sports scores:</b> the Sport features request scores from ESPN’s public scoreboards and from our site. Those providers receive your IP address and basic browser details.</li>\n<li><b>Chess engine and fonts:</b> these run on your device. They send nothing anywhere.</li></ul>\n<p>These providers handle information under their own privacy policies. Some of them are located outside Australia, mainly in the United States.</p>\n\n<h3>5. Why we use information</h3>\n<p>Only to run the features you choose: to let you play, to connect you with other players, to keep your progress and to keep the Service secure and fair.\nFor users in the EU and UK, our lawful bases are performing our agreement with you (the Terms) and our legitimate interest in running a secure, fair service.</p>\n\n<h3>6. Children</h3>\n<p>Kids mode and play against the computer work without sending personal information anywhere. Online features and accounts are for people aged 13 or over, and under-18s need a parent or guardian’s permission.\nWe do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you think a child has given us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>\n\n<h3>7. Security and keeping information</h3>\n<p>Connections use encryption (HTTPS and encrypted WebRTC). Information on your device stays there until you delete it. Account information is kept until you ask us to delete your account.</p>\n\n<h3>8. Your rights</h3>\n<p>You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, and (in the EU and UK) to restrict or object to its use or to receive a copy.\nIf you are not happy with how we handle a request, you can complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au), or to your local data protection authority.</p>\n\n<h3>9. Changes</h3>\n<p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the current version.</p>\n\n<h3>10. Contact</h3>\n<p>Privacy questions and requests: the contact address published on this page (a dedicated address for notices is being set up; until then, watch elitechess.online for it).</p>", "copyright": "<p class=\"lg-date\">Effective 18 October 2026</p>\n<p><b>© 2026 Elite Chess. All rights reserved.</b></p>\n<p>The Elite Chess app and website, including its software, characters, piece sets, boards, artwork, animations, themes, icons, lessons, text and design, are original works owned by Elite Chess\nand are protected by the <i>Copyright Act 1968</i> (Cth) and, through the Berne Convention and other treaties, by copyright law in almost every country.\nNo part may be copied, reproduced, adapted, published, distributed or used to train artificial intelligence without our prior written permission, except as the Terms of Use or a law that cannot be excluded allows.</p>\n\n<h3>Trade marks</h3>\n<p>Elite Chess™, Tournament Wood™, the Elite Chess logo and app icon are trade marks of Elite Chess. You may not use them, or anything confusingly similar,\nfor any product, service, app, domain or account without our written permission.</p>\n\n<h3>Permission requests</h3>\n<p>To ask to use any of our content (for example for a review, a news article or a school), write to us at the contact address published on this page (a dedicated address for notices is being set up; until then, watch elitechess.online for it), describing what you want to use and how. Permission is only given in writing.</p>\n\n<h3>Reporting copying of our work</h3>\n<p>If you see our characters, art, code or app copied or sold elsewhere, please tell us at the contact address published on this page (a dedicated address for notices is being set up; until then, watch elitechess.online for it), with a link and screenshots. We take action against infringements,\nincluding notices to app stores, hosts and marketplaces, and court proceedings.</p>\n\n<h3>If you think we have used your work</h3>\n<p>We respect other people’s rights. If you believe something in the Service infringes your copyright or trade mark, send a notice to the contact address published on this page (a dedicated address for notices is being set up; until then, watch elitechess.online for it) with: your name and contact details;\nthe work you own; where it appears in the Service; a statement that you believe in good faith the use is not authorised; and a statement that your notice is accurate and that you own\nthe rights or may act for the owner. We will look into it promptly and remove or change material where appropriate.</p>\n\n<h3>Third-party parts</h3>\n<p>Some parts of the Service belong to others and are used under open licences: the Stockfish engine (GNU GPL v3), some optional piece sets (GPL, MIT, Apache 2.0, CC BY 4.0 and CC0),\nthe puzzle and opening data (CC0), the recorded sounds (CC0) and the fonts (SIL Open Font License). They are credited, with their full licence texts, in the app under Legal → Credits.\nThose parts are not claimed as ours, and their licences continue to apply to them.</p>\n\n<h3>Not affiliated</h3>\n<p>Elite Chess is independent. It is not affiliated with, sponsored or endorsed by FIDE, lichess.org, Chess.com, the Stockfish project, or any sports league, team, event, competition or organiser.\nNames of events, teams, leagues and players appear only to identify them and belong to their owners. The sports themes are generic and use no official logos.</p>"};
